Native Mark Shot source packages contain four upstream components:

- orig: the exact native Git commit
- orig-vendor: Linux Cargo dependencies selected from the unchanged Cargo.lock
- orig-media: FFmpeg, OpenH264 and nv-codec-headers source files with a SHA-256 manifest
- orig-reference-fonts: byte-pinned Noto Sans 2.015 reference archive and its OFL notice,
  used only to reproduce the Qt geometry fixtures without network access

The build does not access the network. Dependency license notices prepared before
the build are in debian/dependency-licenses. debian/source-commit identifies the
upstream revision. Qt source archives and Qt v* release tags are not supported.

Ubuntu 26.04 currently supplies Rust 1.93.1. Launchpad requires a configured
build-dependency source supplying rustc and cargo >= 1.95 before PPA upload.
CI verifies the actual Rustup 1.99.1 toolchain separately from all dpkg-managed
system dependencies; the original source package retains its strict Rust
Build-Depends constraints. Builds use the default dynamic CPU OCR feature.
The OCR runtime and models remain explicit user downloads, not build inputs.
